  "question": {
    "text": "In the figure shown below, a resistance of $150.4 \\Omega$ is connected in series to an ammeter A of resistance $240 \\Omega$. A shunt resistance of $10 \\Omega$ is connected in parallel with the ammeter. The reading of the ammeter is _____ mA.<br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0026_9cf7483b5da0.png\"/>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0026_2264e6d32948.png\"/><br/><img src=\"assets\\st0026_cd2b42f4391e.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=\\mathrm{R}_1+\\mathrm{R}_2 \\\\ & \\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=150.4+\\frac{240 \\times 10}{250} \\\\ & =150.4+9.6=160 \\Omega \\\\ & \\mathrm{I}_1=\\frac{\\mathrm{I} \\mathrm{R}_2}{240} \\\\ & \\mathrm{I}_1=\\frac{\\mathrm{I} \\times 9.6}{240} \\\\ & =\\frac{20}{160} \\times \\frac{9.6}{2400}=\\frac{1}{200}=5 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~A}=5 \\mathrm{~mA}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}